%% Source: 02-cross-cutting-flows.md - 2.2 Transactional outbox and inbox
sequenceDiagram
    participant S as Domain service
    participant DB as Postgres
    participant O as Outbox relay worker
    participant Q as Queue
    participant C as Consumer
    participant I as Consumer inbox table

    S->>DB: BEGIN
    S->>DB: write domain change
    S->>DB: insert outbox event
    S->>DB: COMMIT
    loop poll or notify
        O->>DB: read unpublished events
        O->>Q: publish event
        O->>DB: mark published
    end
    Q->>C: deliver event
    C->>I: insert event_id if absent
    alt already processed
        C-->>Q: ack and skip
    else first time
        C->>C: handle event
        C->>I: mark processed
        C-->>Q: ack
    end
